title: "Poisson SuSiE across the background rate"
subtitle: "gIBSS-GO, gIBSS-Q2, gIBSS-Laplace and score against CAVI-Q2 as the baseline rate runs from 0.01 to 100, on Gaussian, binary and nested block designs (experiment 025)."
engine: jupyter
jupyter: python3
execute:
  fig-dpi: 110
---


## Design

Counts $y_i \sim \text{Poisson}(\exp(b_0 + x_i^\top \beta))$ with background rate $\lambda_0 = e^{b_0} \in \{0.01, 0.1, 1, 10, 100\}$.
Each causal effect is calibrated to $E[\text{LRT}] = T \in \{8, 12, 16, 20, 24\}$ for its own column at that rate (`calibrate_rate.py`), so detectability is matched along $\lambda_0$.

- Multi-effect: 3 equal causals, `gap` 8 (correlated) or 64 (independent) columns apart, fit $L = 5$.
- Single effect (`-ser`): one causal at column 64, fit $L = 1$.
- Arms, all scored in Q2 with an EB prior variance: CAVI-Q2 (exact closed-form offset, up to 500 sweeps), gIBSS-GO (Gaussian offset: gIBSS-Q2 with each leave-one-out offset replaced by a moment-matched Gaussian surrogate and integrated over in closed form, $E[e^{o}] = e^{m + V/2}$; $L = 5$ only), gIBSS-Q2 (plug-in mean offset), gIBSS-Laplace (order-1 quadrature SER, plug-in offset, reduced to Q2), score (one Newton step from the intercept-only null).
- 200 replicates per cell. Declared = 95% CS of a component with SER log BF $\geq 2$.

| design | $X$ | causal set size |
|---|---|---|
| gaussian | AR1 Gaussian, $n = 500$, $p = 256$, $\rho = 0.9$ | dense |
| binary | binary Markov, $n = 1000$, $p = 256$, corr 0.8, density 0.1 | ~100 |
| block | nested attrition (024's), $n = 1000$, causals at depth 3 | ~83 |

Figure rows, each relative to CAVI-Q2 on the same simulated data:
**coverage** = arm minus CAVI fraction of declared CSs containing a causal;
**power** = arm minus CAVI fraction of causals inside some declared CS;
**CS size ratio** = mean declared-CS size, arm over CAVI;
**ELBO** = arm minus CAVI common Q2 ELBO, mean per fit (score omitted: its Q2 ELBO reaches about $-10^{15}$ at $\lambda_0 = 0.01$).
Bands are 95% CIs from resampling replicates jointly for both arms.
gIBSS-GO runs away on 3 of the 22,000 binary and block signal fits (8,600 to 39,000 nats below CAVI; several components stacked on one column with effects in the hundreds, prior variance at its cap). These three fits cause the ELBO dips at binary $T = 16$ gap 64 $\lambda_0 = 0.01$ and block $T = 24$.

PIP agreement figures: each arm's components are matched to CAVI-Q2's on the same replicate by minimum total TV (Hungarian; identity at $L = 1$).
x = TV between a matched pair's $\alpha$ vectors; y = share of matched pairs with TV above x.
Rows bar on the pair's smaller component log BF (both sides must clear it). Non-null cells, pooled over $T$ and gap; TV below $10^{-4}$ is drawn at $10^{-4}$.

Conditional figures compare the effect size given its feature, $q(b \mid \gamma = j) = N(\mu_j, \sigma_j^2)$, on the same matched pairs, averaged over CAVI-Q2's $\alpha$:
$|\Delta\mu| / \sigma = \sum_j \alpha_j |\mu'_j - \mu_j| / \sigma_j$ (shift in CAVI-Q2 posterior SDs) and $|\log \sigma'/\sigma|$ with $\log \sigma'/\sigma = \sum_j \alpha_j \log(\sigma'_j/\sigma_j)$.
Pairs whose smaller component log BF exceeds 2 only; below that the conditionals sit near the prior.
An arm that matches CAVI-Q2's $\alpha$ and these conditionals reproduces the whole single-effect posterior.

Table columns, CAVI-Q2's own values pooled over $T$:
**coverage** = covering / declared CSs;
**power** = captured causals / causals;
**mean CS size** = mean size of declared CSs;
**declared CSs** = count over all reps;
**reps** = replicate fits pooled.

## All scenarios

Coverage, power, mean size and number per fit of declared 95% CSs, one point per signal scenario (design, $\lambda_0$, $T$, gap): 150 scenarios per arm at $L = 5$, 75 at $L = 1$.

